@@ -0,0 +1,34 @@
+# Product review research
+
+## Request flow and data model
+
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/api/v1/product/ProductReviewApi.java` owns the v1 review endpoints. The public GET delegates to `ProductCommonFacade.getProductReviews`. POST currently checks duplicate reviews using `review.getProductId()` before assigning the path `{id}`, checks only an upper bound, and converts all failures to 503. PUT/DELETE look up by review id, but PUT checks the submitted customer rather than the URL product and DELETE is the only operation that checks product ownership.
+- `PersistableProductReview` and `ProductReviewEntity` expose rating as `Double`; Bean Validation has `@Min(1)`/`@Max(5)`, which permits fractional values. The existing tests also construct ratings as doubles, so whole-number validation should be added without changing the Java setter type.
+- `/api/v1/auth/**` is protected by the customer security configuration and the JWT filter. The authenticated principal is `JWTUser`, which exposes the authenticated customer id via `getId()`. The request body must therefore be compared with that id before any persistence work.
+- `ProductReview` has a unique database constraint on `(CUSTOMERS_ID, PRODUCT_ID)`, a customer/product association, and cascaded descriptions. `ProductReviewRepository` already provides `findByProductAndCustomer` and product review queries.
+
+## Privacy defect
+
+- `ReadableProductReview` contains a `ReadableCustomer customer` field.
+- `ReadableProductReviewPopulator` invokes `ReadableCustomerPopulator`, which fills the complete customer DTO, including email, billing and delivery addresses and other customer fields. This is the source of the public data leak. The public response needs a review-specific minimal reviewer representation containing only `firstName` (while retaining the existing `customer` response shape for compatibility).
+
+## Rating defects
+
+- `ProductReviewServiceImpl.saveOrUpdate` starts with the product's cached average/count, adds the incoming rating, and increments the count for both create and update. It never calculates from the actual review rows, so edits inflate the count and average.
+- The inherited delete operation removes only the review. `ProductReviewServiceImpl` has no delete override, so product average/count remain stale after deletion and do not become zero when the final review is removed.
+- Product read mapping in `ReadableProductMapper` copies `Product.productReviewAvg` and `productReviewCount` to the v2 response. It rounds the average to the nearest half, not the requested one decimal place with halves rounded up. The service must persist a one-decimal `BigDecimal` using `RoundingMode.HALF_UP`; the read mapper should preserve that value and provide zero defaults.
+- `ProductServiceImpl.deleteProduct` explicitly deletes product reviews through the review service, so a corrected review delete path also affects product deletion and must recalculate safely when reviews are removed.
+
+## Files expected to change
+
+- v1 API controller for status codes, path ownership, authenticated-customer authorization, and validation behavior.
+- Review DTO/response model and public review populator for minimal reviewer data and whole-number validation.
+- Product review service/repository for transactional recalculation after create, update, and delete.
+- Product read mapper for exact one-decimal rating and zero/no-review defaults.
+- Focused integration/unit tests if the existing test setup permits them; existing product-management tests cover the older private POST contract and should remain compilable.
+
+## Other affected behavior
+
+- The private merchant review POST remains available, so validation and recalculation must work for both merchant creation and authenticated customer creation.
+- PUT should update the existing review by id rather than create a new row, preserve its customer/product associations, and return 404 for an absent or cross-product review.
+- Rejected customer submissions must return before the facade/service is called, ensuring no review or product aggregate is written.
